Whether post-Labor Day polling confirms the August tightening or reverts to the state's Republican baseline.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Tom Cotton (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Senator Tom Cotton seeks reelection in a state that backed Republicans by about 15 points in recent cycles. He enters with roughly $9.9 million on hand against about $0.9 million for Democrat Hallie Shoffner, a former venture capitalist and farmer who has drawn attention and some outside spending against Cotton. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nPolling has been sparse and mixed: one August survey showed Shoffner narrowly ahead, while others had Cotton up by 5 to 16 points. Prediction markets still price Cotton around 93 to 95 percent, and every major race rater places the contest in the Safe or Solid Republican column. The race appears likely to stay comfortably in Cotton's column, with the main question being the final margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0277, "margin": -11.06}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0629, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.052, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0436, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0489, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0435, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.061, "margin": -10.5}]}